editor.nod_help.page.examples=Ejemplos
editor.nod_help.page.troubleshooting=Errores comunes


editor.nod_help.chg.extra=<h2>Ejemplos chg</h2><p><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:chg"><code>chg</code></a> cambia el inicio del texto o un patrÃ³n. Sirve para telÃ©fonos, cÃ³digos, prefijos y tablas de renumeraciÃ³n.</p><div class="notice"><b>Estructura:</b> izquierda = lo que se busca, derecha = nueva forma. Usa comillas para espacios, comas o caracteres especiales.</div><details open><summary>Reemplazar prefijo</summary><table><tr><th>Objetivo</th><th>Regla</th><th>Ejemplo</th></tr><tr><td>Prefix</td><td><code>chg "01751","07051"</code></td><td><code>0175112345</code> -> <code>0705112345</code></td></tr><tr><td>Dash</td><td><code>chg "01751-","070-51"</code></td><td><code>01751-12345</code> -> <code>070-5112345</code></td></tr></table></details><details><summary>PatrÃ³n con x</summary><p>NOD 2.0: <code>x</code> captura un dÃ­gito y lo vuelve a colocar a la derecha. Los espacios y guiones de la izquierda son solo para lectura.</p><pre>chg "0183x-xx xx","0183-x0 xx xx"</pre><p><code>01835-1234</code> -> <code>0183-501234</code>.</p></details><details><summary>Errores comunes</summary><ul><li>Pon las reglas especÃ­ficas encima de las generales.</li><li>No olvides la coma.</li><li>Usa <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:trans"><code>trans</code></a> para traducir un valor completo.</li></ul></details>
editor.nod_help.math.extra=<h2>Math en resumen</h2><p><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:math"><code>math</code></a> calcula con <code>ans</code>. En la primera lÃ­nea <code>ans</code> es el valor de entrada; despuÃ©s es el resultado anterior.</p><div class="notice"><b>Estructura:</b> elige primero el tipo de cÃ¡lculo y luego escribe la syntax correcta. Para fÃ³rmulas grandes, usa parÃ©ntesis o varias lÃ­neas <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:math"><code>math</code></a>.</div><div class="math-flow"><span class="math-pill">1. Operaciones bÃ¡sicas</span><span class="math-pill">2. Funciones y constantes</span><span class="math-pill">3. FÃ³rmulas complejas</span><span class="math-pill">4. CÃ¡lculo: diff, integral, lÃ­mite</span></div><details open><summary>Operaciones bÃ¡sicas</summary><table><tr><th>Objetivo</th><th>Syntax</th><th>Ejemplo</th></tr><tr><td>+</td><td><code>math ans + number</code></td><td><code>math ans + 32</code></td></tr><tr><td>-</td><td><code>math ans - number</code></td><td><code>math ans - 10</code></td></tr><tr><td>*</td><td><code>math ans * factor</code></td><td><code>math ans * 1.8</code></td></tr><tr><td>/</td><td><code>math ans / factor</code></td><td><code>math ans / 1.95583</code></td></tr></table><pre>Name Euro to cents&#13;&#10;input1 Euro&#13;&#10;input2 Cents&#13;&#10;format #.00&#13;&#10;math ans * 100&#13;&#10;end</pre></details><details><summary>Funciones y constantes</summary><table><tr><th>Groep</th><th>Syntax</th><th>Nota</th></tr><tr><td>Power</td><td><code>math ans^2</code> or <code>math pow(ans,3)</code></td><td>Square, cube.</td></tr><tr><td>Root</td><td><code>math sqrt(ans)</code></td><td>Can be used inside formulas.</td></tr><tr><td>Pi/e</td><td><code>math pi * ans^2</code><br><code>math e^ans</code></td><td>Circle and exponential.</td></tr><tr><td>Degrees</td><td><code>math sind(ans)</code><br><code>math cosd(ans)</code></td><td>Use <code>sin/cos/tan</code> for radians.</td></tr></table></details><details><summary>FÃ³rmulas complejas</summary><p>Usa parÃ©ntesis cuando el orden sea importante. Escribe siempre la multiplicaciÃ³n con <code>*</code>.</p><pre>math sqrt(ans^2 + 25)&#13;&#10;math ((ans + 10) * 2) / 3&#13;&#10;math ans * (1 + 0.04)^5</pre><h3>Ejemplo: PitÃ¡goras</h3><div class="mathml-formula"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="inline"><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>5</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt></mrow></math></div><pre>Name Hypotenuse&#13;&#10;input1 Side a&#13;&#10;input2 Side c&#13;&#10;format #.00&#13;&#10;math sqrt(ans^2 + 25)&#13;&#10;end</pre><p>AquÃ­ <code>ans</code> es el lado <code>a</code>; el otro lado queda fijo en <code>5</code>.</p></details><details><summary>CÃ¡lculo: diff, integral, lÃ­mite</summary><table><tr><th>Objetivo</th><th>Syntax</th><th>Resultado</th></tr><tr><td>Derivative</td><td><code>math diff ans^2</code></td><td>Pendiente numÃ©rica.</td></tr><tr><td>Integral</td><td><code>math integral 0,1 ans^2</code></td><td>Ãrea numÃ©rica de 0 a 1.</td></tr><tr><td>Limit</td><td><code>math limit 0 sin(ans)/ans</code></td><td>AproximaciÃ³n alrededor de 0.</td></tr></table></details><h2>Errores comunes</h2><ul><li>No olvides <code>ans</code>.</li><li>Usa <code>sind</code> para grados.</li><li>Usa <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:reverse"><code>reverse</code></a> para conversiÃ³n inversa compleja.</li></ul>
editor.nod_help.mode.extra=<h2>CuÃ¡ndo usar mode?</h2><p><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:mode"><code>mode</code></a> indica quÃ© tipo de archivo NOD estÃ¡s creando. Para un convertidor normal, normalmente no hace falta.</p><div class="notice"><b>Estructura:</b> usa <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:mode"><code>mode</code></a> solo para tipos especiales, como procesamiento de datos o resoluciÃ³n de ecuaciones.</div><details open><summary>Modes</summary><table><tr><th>Mode</th><th>CuÃ¡ndo</th><th>Comandos</th></tr><tr><td><code>mode calculator</code></td><td>Convertidor normal</td><td><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:math"><code>math</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:trans"><code>trans</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:chg"><code>chg</code></a></td></tr><tr><td><code>mode data</code></td><td>Procesamiento de datos</td><td><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:table"><code>table</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:field"><code>field</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:output"><code>output</code></a></td></tr><tr><td><code>mode equation</code></td><td>Resolver ecuaciÃ³n</td><td><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:given"><code>given</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:equation"><code>equation</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:solve"><code>solve</code></a></td></tr></table></details><details><summary>Ejemplo: converter</summary><pre>Name Celsius to Fahrenheit&#13;&#10;input1 Celsius&#13;&#10;input2 Fahrenheit&#13;&#10;format #.00&#13;&#10;math ans * 1.8&#13;&#10;math ans + 32&#13;&#10;end</pre></details><details><summary>Ejemplo: equation</summary><pre>Name Solve equation&#13;&#10;mode equation&#13;&#10;given y = 20&#13;&#10;equation y = x * 2&#13;&#10;solve x&#13;&#10;constraint x >= 0&#13;&#10;end</pre></details>
editor.nod_help.trans.extra=<h2>Ejemplos trans</h2><p><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:trans"><code>trans</code></a> traduce un valor completo. Ãšsalo para palabras, cÃ³digos fijos, estados, cÃ³digos postales y listas cortas.</p><div class="notice"><b>Estructura:</b> <code>trans "old value","new value"</code>. La entrada completa debe coincidir con el valor de la izquierda.</div><details open><summary>Traducir texto exacto</summary><table><tr><th>Objetivo</th><th>Regla</th><th>Resultado</th></tr><tr><td>Word</td><td><code>trans "hallo","hello"</code></td><td><code>hallo</code> -> <code>hello</code></td></tr><tr><td>Status</td><td><code>trans "open","in progress"</code></td><td><code>open</code> -> <code>in progress</code></td></tr><tr><td>Address</td><td><code>trans "2566 GB 241","Nieboerweg 241, 2566 GB Den Haag"</code></td><td>postcode + house number -> address</td></tr></table></details><details><summary>trans / chg</summary><table><tr><th>Comando</th><th>CuÃ¡ndo</th><th>Ejemplo</th></tr><tr><td><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:trans"><code>trans</code></a></td><td>La entrada completa se conoce exactamente.</td><td><code>hallo</code> -> <code>hello</code></td></tr><tr><td><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:chg"><code>chg</code></a></td><td>Solo cambia el inicio o el patrÃ³n.</td><td><code>01751-xxxxx</code> -> <code>070-51xxxxx</code></td></tr></table></details><details><summary>Errores comunes</summary><ul><li>Izquierda es entrada, derecha es salida.</li><li>Usa <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:chg"><code>chg</code></a> para cambios parciales.</li><li>Evita traducciones duplicadas para la misma entrada.</li></ul></details>
editor.nod_help.full.classic=<h2>IntroducciÃ³n al editor NOD</h2><p>El editor NOD es el espacio de trabajo de los convertidores. El cÃ³digo estÃ¡ arriba, las pruebas abajo y la vista previa a la derecha muestra etiquetas, sÃ­mbolos, texto introductorio y resultados.</p><h2>ClÃ¡sico 1.73 y NOD 2.0</h2><table><tr><th>Syscalculator 1.73 / NOD 1.0</th><th>Syscalculator 2.0 / editor NOD</th></tr><tr><td>Archivos de texto clÃ¡sicos con <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:name"><code>Name</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:input1"><code>input1</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:input2"><code>input2</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:math"><code>math</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:trans"><code>trans</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:chg"><code>chg</code></a> y <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:end"><code>end</code></a>.</td><td>La misma base sigue compatible con archivos NOD antiguos.</td></tr><tr><td>La posiciÃ³n de sÃ­mbolos a menudo debÃ­a recordarse y probarse.</td><td>La vista previa muestra al instante <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:symb1"><code>Symb1</code></a> hasta <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:symb4"><code>Symb4</code></a>.</td></tr><tr><td><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:chg"><code>chg</code></a> era sobre todo reemplazo de prefijo.</td><td><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:chg"><code>chg</code></a> sigue compatible; NOD 2.0 aÃ±ade patrones con captura <code>x</code>.</td></tr><tr><td>La ayuda venÃ­a sobre todo de ejemplos.</td><td>El editor ofrece sugerencias, ayuda con clic derecho y pÃ¡ginas de ejemplos.</td></tr></table><h2>Sintaxis: vista completa de NOD 1.0 y NOD 2.0</h2><p>Esta tabla muestra quÃ© sintaxis viene de los archivos NOD clÃ¡sicos y quÃ© se aÃ±adiÃ³ en NOD 2.0.</p><table class="syntax-compare"><tr><th>Syntax / feature</th><th>NOD 1.0</th><th>NOD 2.0</th><th>Note</th></tr><tr><td><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:name"><code>Name</code></a></td><td><span class="yes">âœ“</span></td><td><span class="yes">âœ“</span></td><td>Converter name/title.</td></tr><tr><td><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:urln"><code>URLN</code></a></td><td><span class="yes">âœ“</span></td><td><span class="yes">âœ“</span></td><td>Reference/source line remains supported.</td></tr><tr><td><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:input1"><code>input1</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:input2"><code>input2</code></a></td><td><span class="yes">âœ“</span></td><td><span class="yes">âœ“</span></td><td>Labels for input and output.</td></tr><tr><td><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:result"><code>Result</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:resfou"><code>Resfou</code></a></td><td><span class="yes">âœ“</span></td><td><span class="yes">âœ“</span></td><td>Result label and error text.</td></tr><tr><td><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:symb1"><code>Symb1</code></a> through <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:symb4"><code>Symb4</code></a></td><td><span class="yes">âœ“</span></td><td><span class="yes">âœ“</span></td><td>Symbols left/right of input and output; NOD 2.0 shows them in preview.</td></tr><tr><td><code>format #.00</code></td><td><span class="yes">âœ“</span></td><td><span class="yes">âœ“</span></td><td>Number formatting stays the same.</td></tr><tr><td><code>mode calculator</code></td><td><span class="no">Ã—</span></td><td><span class="yes">âœ“</span></td><td>NOD 2.0 uses <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:mode"><code>mode</code></a> for special file types; normal converters also work without mode.</td></tr><tr><td><code>mode data</code></td><td><span class="no">Ã—</span></td><td><span class="yes">âœ“</span></td><td>For table/field processing.</td></tr><tr><td><code>mode equation</code></td><td><span class="no">Ã—</span></td><td><span class="yes">âœ“</span></td><td>For solving equations with <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:given"><code>given</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:equation"><code>equation</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:solve"><code>solve</code></a>.</td></tr><tr><td><code>math ans * 1.8</code></td><td><span class="yes">âœ“</span></td><td><span class="yes">âœ“</span></td><td>Classic calculation with <code>ans</code>.</td></tr><tr><td><code>math sqrt(ans^2 + 25)</code></td><td><span class="no">Ã—</span></td><td><span class="yes">âœ“</span></td><td>Richer formulas and functions in NOD 2.0.</td></tr><tr><td><code>chg "01751-","070-51"</code></td><td><span class="yes">âœ“</span></td><td><span class="yes">âœ“</span></td><td>Classic prefix replacement keeps working.</td></tr><tr><td><code>chg "0183x-xx xx","0183-x0 xx xx"</code></td><td><span class="no">Ã—</span></td><td><span class="yes">âœ“</span></td><td>New in NOD 2.0: pattern with <code>x</code> capture.</td></tr><tr><td><code>trans "old","new"</code></td><td><span class="yes">âœ“</span></td><td><span class="yes">âœ“</span></td><td>Exact text translation remains compatible.</td></tr><tr><td><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:reverse"><code>reverse</code></a></td><td><span class="yes">âœ“</span></td><td><span class="yes">âœ“</span></td><td>Reverse direction of a converter.</td></tr><tr><td><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:table"><code>table</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:field"><code>field</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:output"><code>output</code></a></td><td><span class="no">Ã—</span></td><td><span class="yes">âœ“</span></td><td>NOD 2.0 data converters with fields and output construction.</td></tr><tr><td><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:phoneformat"><code>phoneformat</code></a></td><td><span class="no">Ã—</span></td><td><span class="yes">âœ“</span></td><td>Format phone numbers in data/number converters.</td></tr><tr><td><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:lookup"><code>lookup</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:match"><code>match</code></a></td><td><span class="no">Ã—</span></td><td><span class="yes">âœ“</span></td><td>Look up tables or connect values.</td></tr><tr><td><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:given"><code>given</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:equation"><code>equation</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:solve"><code>solve</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:constraint"><code>constraint</code></a></td><td><span class="no">Ã—</span></td><td><span class="yes">âœ“</span></td><td>Solve equations with constraints.</td></tr><tr><td><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:preview"><code>preview</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:backup"><code>backup</code></a></td><td><span class="no">Ã—</span></td><td><span class="yes">âœ“</span></td><td>Editor/safety information for NOD 2.0 files.</td></tr><tr><td><code>indoprint ... indoend</code></td><td><span class="yes">âœ“</span></td><td><span class="yes">âœ“</span></td><td>Introduction text remains supported.</td></tr><tr><td><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:end"><code>end</code></a></td><td><span class="yes">âœ“</span></td><td><span class="yes">âœ“</span></td><td>Closes the NOD file.</td></tr><tr><td>Live preview, suggestions, right-click help</td><td><span class="no">Ã—</span></td><td><span class="yes">âœ“</span></td><td>This is editor help, not old runtime syntax.</td></tr></table><h2>Lo que sigue igual</h2><ul><li>Comandos legibles por lÃ­nea.</li><li><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:end"><code>end</code></a> cierra el archivo.</li><li>Un convertidor simple sigue siendo corto.</li></ul><h2>Lo nuevo</h2><ul><li>Vista previa en vivo y simulador.</li><li>Graph 2D para grÃ¡ficos de convertidores math.</li><li>Sugerencias al escribir.</li><li>Ayuda mÃ¡s completa por comando.</li><li>MÃ¡s ejemplos para <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:math"><code>math</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:trans"><code>trans</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:chg"><code>chg</code></a>, sÃ­mbolos e <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:indoprint"><code>indoprint</code></a>.</li></ul>
